  pi(A) = 0.3446
  pi(C) = 0.1304
  pi(G) = 0.09982
  pi(T) = 0.4251

Rate matrix Q:

  A   -0.6484   0.06597    0.2918    0.2906
  C    0.1743    -2.217   0.06782     1.975
  G     1.007   0.08861    -1.197    0.1013
  T    0.2355    0.6059    0.0238   -0.8652

Model of rate heterogeneity: Gamma with 4 categories
Gamma shape alpha: 0.3302

 Category  Relative_rate  Proportion
  1         0.00806        0.25
  2         0.1281         0.25
  3         0.6432         0.25
  4         3.221          0.25
Relative rates are computed as MEAN of the portion of the Gamma distribution falling in the category.

